Q: How to make the animation on a web site where a piece of text changes every seconds? A: <p>This is basic idea how to create this kind of animation check following snippet:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>If you want to expend this animation just add letters in array.</p>
</blockquote>

<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>$(function() {
	var arr = ['t','te','tex','text','G','Go','Goo','Goog','Googl','Googl','Google'];
  var elem = $('#ani');
  var i = 0;
  var loop = function(){
  	elem.text(arr[i++]);
    if(i&gt;arr.length) {
    	//clearInterval(intervalID);
        i=0;
      }
  }
  
  var intervalID = setInterval(loop, 500);
})</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.test{
  font-size:26px;
  color:green;
}
.ani{
  color:red;
}
.ani::after{
  content:"|";
  -webkit-animation: cursor-blink 0.8s linear infinite;
  -moz-animation: cursor-blink 0.8s linear infinite;
  -o-animation: cursor-blink 0.8s linear infinite;
  animation: cursor-blink 0.8s linear infinite;
}

@-moz-keyframes cursor-blink {
  1% {
    opacity: 0;
  }
  40% {
    opacity: 0;
  }
  60% {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  100% {
    opacity: 1;
  }
}
@-webkit-keyframes cursor-blink {
  1% {
    opacity: 0;
  }
  40% {
    opacity: 0;
  }
  60% {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  100% {
    opacity: 1;
  }
}
@-o-keyframes cursor-blink {
  1% {
    opacity: 0;
  }
  40% {
    opacity: 0;
  }
  60% {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  100% {
    opacity: 1;
  }
}
@keyframes cursor-blink {
  1% {
    opacity: 0;
  }
  40% {
    opacity: 0;
  }
  60% {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  100% {
    opacity: 1;
  }
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="test"&gt;
  This is text 
  &lt;span class="ani" id="ani"&gt;
   Google
  &lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;script src="//code.jquery.com/jquery-1.11.3.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
